{
  "description": "#6741 — a list as one line of text in the Edit as Markdown buffer, in Duplicate and in a template's batch. Under a key that holds a list a block's `key:: a, b` line is the list's text (`write_property_list`), and the page's own front matter line a YAML list (`key: [a, \"b, c\"]`): an item holding a comma is quoted, a number is its digits. The page's own buffer saves as nothing; a changed line writes the list it reads as (`property_list_items`), each item under the item type; a number list item that is no number refuses the whole save. Duplicate copies the block's lists item for item, one under an undeclared key too, though its line alone reads as text; a YAML list under an undeclared key is a list, and a `create_blocks_batch` spec's typed property takes a list. A text under a key that holds a list is written as a list of one, so its line reads back as one item, not as the parts its comma splits it into. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
